; Stage 15 W8 G-1: a call is still not a constant. Partly SUPERSEDED by G-3 —
; see the note below the two forms, which is why the subject is now an aggregate
; ELEMENT rather than the scalar slot this fixture originally used.
(defn g1-f (x:i32):i32 (return x))
(defvar g1-arr:(array i32 2) (array i32 1 (+ 1 (g1-f 2))))

; G-3 (design/global-init.md §5) made the ORIGINAL subject of this fixture —
; `(defvar g1-nc:i32 (+ 1 (g1-f 2)))` — legal: at a scalar slot it is a RUNTIME
; initializer, queued for @__nucleus_init, and examples/g3-runtime-init.nuc runs
; exactly that shape and prints the value. What still carries this diagnostic,
; and must, is an aggregate element: an LLVM aggregate constant is filled at
; link time and there is no `set!` that could fill one slot of it, so `(array T
; …)` stays constant-only. The subject changed; the message and the `:5:` the
; harness asserts did not.
